  "surprise": "P19 reversed (cosine floor 0.1 -> 0.3) is a wash downstream and costs RL wall-clock. Seeds 370/308/382 (mean 353.33) versus 070-claude 359/335/364 (mean 352.67): the recorded rounded metric ties at 353, and a same-complexity constant change does not win a tie, so discard; the +0.67 unrounded gap is far inside seed noise (spread 308-382 is wider than 070's 335-364). As predicted, pretraining ended less annealed: val loss 0.0940/0.0968/0.0916 (mean 0.0941, +1.4% versus 0.0928) and held-out greedy fell from 0.987-0.9875 to 0.9695-0.976. The surprise is where that shows up: the less-annealed handoff was a worse RL starting point, with round-1 solves 172/97/269 (mean 179) versus 200/324/206 (mean 243) and round-1 sampling at 296/399/291 samples/s versus 428/560/563 (round 1 took 213/165/221 s versus 164/139/140 s), consistent with more long no-QED samples at T=0.8. RL mostly caught up by round 4 (RL solved 795/703/852, mean 783 versus 803) and eval landed level. Total seconds 1147/983/1199 versus 1048/971/1079 exceeded my +60 s prediction; seed 2 finished 1 s under the 1200 s SIGALRM, so keeping this floor would push later experiments toward timeouts. With 016's floor-to-zero loss (AdamW era), the downstream metric looks flat to slightly peaked near a 0.1 floor, not monotone in plasticity; the WD gains of 069/070 are not a schedule-endpoint effect that a higher floor can extend.",
